    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm looking at a 2022 Ford F-150 that's slipping under load. I'm running a diagnostic scan and I'm seeing some really irregular pressure spikes in the hydraulic circuit. What are the most likely culprits for these kind of fluctuations in an automatic transmission?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Irregular pressure spikes in a hydraulic circuit on an automatic transmission, especially when under load, can be a serious sign of internal issues. The most likely culprits are a worn or clogged transmission filter, a failing solenoid, or issues with the transmission fluid itself. You might also be looking at a problem with the torque converter clutch or internal valve body wear. It's best to have a professional mechanic diagnose the exact source of the erratic pressure before driving it further.",
